sumed by:\\n  - MCP path: `server.py:1407 _respond(BacklogAddResponse, {**result, ...})` -> `BacklogAddResponse` inherits `error` from `FallibleToolResponse` (tool_responses.py:212-228); `_respond` uses `model_validate` on the full payload dict (not an allowlist), so `error` survives to the wire [CONNECTED]\\n  - CLI path: `sam_schema/backlog.py:76-78` `_emit(result, output); if result.get(\\\"error\\\"): raise typer.Exit(code=1)` [CONNECTED]\\n- Test wiring: `test_backlog_core_operations.py::test_add_item_error_set_when_issue_creation_raises` and `::test_add_item_item_ref_empty_when_no_github_issue` import `add_item` from the real module and patch the real `try_get_github`/`create_issue_for_item` symbols (not a local stub) -- ran all 3 relevant tests live: `3 passed in 6.19s` [CONNECTED, data flow verified by execution, not just static trace]\\n- Doc: `work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` Step 5 (lines 157-170) and Completion criteria (lines 198-209) correctly disambiguate: error+reference-present = stored-but-failed (continue), error+no-reference = never-stored (stop) [CONNECTED]\\n\\nGAPS:\\n  Gap 1: BROKEN_FLOW - interop skill's backlog-item-creation step does not handle the new stored-but-failed outcome\\n    - File: plugins/development-harness/skills/interop/SKILL.md:91-95 (Step 3 mermaid flowchart)\\n    - Flow: `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_add` -> \\\"Response has error key?\\\" -> Yes -> \\\"ABORT ERROR: Failed to create backlog item\\\"\\n    - Breaks at: this is a second, independent consumer of `backlog_add`'s response contract (T5's task body claimed \\\"Impact Radius confirmed no other consumer\\\" of `item_ref`/`error`; that claim does not hold -- this file was in scope of the `grep -rn 'backlog_add'` sweep but its `error`-handling branch was not caught by the narrower `item_ref`-only grep the T5 CoVe check used).\\n    - Reason: before #3182, `error` on `backlog_add` could only appear when the item was never created (duplicate/validation failure) -- \\\"ABORT, make no changes\\\" was correct. After #3182, `error` can also appear when the item WAS created locally (issue-creation-failed branch: `item_ref==\\\"\\\"`, `reference` populated, `error` populated). This flow now aborts unconditionally on any `error`, without checking `reference`, on a call that already has side effects (a stored backlog item) -- the same contradiction T5 fixed in `create/start.md` Step 5, uncorrected here. Net effect: the plan file's `**Backlog item:** #N` line is never written and the newly created local-only item is silently orphaned from the plan file the interop workflow is trying to link.\\n    - Fix: mirror `create/start.md`'s Step 5 disambiguation -- branch on `error` AND (`reference`/`file_path`/`title` present) vs `error` with none present; on the stored-but-failed case, do not abort, report the error, and (since this flow's downstream step only knows how to write a `#N` issue number, not a bare `reference`) either extend `WriteRef` to accept a `reference` fallback or explicitly document this as a follow-up gap for `interop/SKILL.md` to close in its own change.\\n\\nCONNECTED_COUNT: 8\\nGAPS_COUNT: 1 (doc-only; no production code path affected)\\nFOLLOW_UP_TASKS:\\n  1. Update `plugins/development-harness/skills/interop/SKILL.md` Step 3 (lines 91-95) to disambiguate stored-but-failed from never-stored, matching `work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` Step 5's pattern (Agent: dh:service-docs-maintainer)\\nNEXT_STEP: Route Gap 1 to a follow-up task before closing out item 3182's quality gate; it does not block T9's PASS verdict (production code, MCP/CLI wiring, and the item's own Acceptance Criteria are all satisfied) but is a real orphaned-item risk for any agent following the interop workflow after this fix ships.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"low\"},{\"id\":\"T4\",\"title\":\"Documentation Drift Audit\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"doc-d